From 223fbb90c2c24d2e210ed7a84ee6fc0cf030e558 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:17:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/30] allwinner: the CPU-level power-down rule holds for
 every native-ops platform

The commit that limited power-down states to the CPU level ("power-down
states at CPU level only, standby from core 0 only") changed common code
under an H713 subject and did not say how far it reaches.
sunxi_validate_power_state serves every Allwinner platform that runs the
native PSCI ops, which have CPU_SUSPEND since "implement PSCI CPU_SUSPEND
for the native power ops". On all of them a cluster-level power-down
state is refused now, where it used to power down the CPU alone, and so
is a system-level one, where it used to reset the board
(sunxi_system_suspend_enter() is -1 without SUNXI_SYSTEM_SUSPEND).

TF-A adds idle states to the device tree only with the SCPI ops, which
validate power states on their own; such a state could come only from a
board's own device tree. Of the other platforms only sun50i_h6 was built
here, none was run. A submission upstream would put the rule behind the
H713 or say this in its own message. The comment says it is common code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
index 5bf772d1d..5887a2aa7 100644
--- a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
+++ b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
@@ -62,7 +62,8 @@ static int sunxi_validate_power_state(unsigned int power_state,
 		 * Only the CPU powers down here. Nothing natively takes the
 		 * cluster or the system down, and a system-level OFF is the
 		 * SYSTEM_SUSPEND hand-over to the management processor: it
-		 * must not be reachable around that call's checks.
+		 * must not be reachable around that call's checks. Common
+		 * code: every platform on the native ops refuses these.
 		 */
 		if (power_level != MPIDR_AFFLVL0) {
 			return PSCI_E_INVALID_PARAMS;
